  "Question": "Margie’s car can go \\(32\\) miles on a gallon of gas, and gas currently costs \\(\\$4\\) per gallon. How many miles can Margie drive on \\(\\$20\\) worth of gas?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 64 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 128 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 160 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 320 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 640 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "First find how much gas \\(\\$20\\) buys. At \\(\\$4\\) per gallon, Margie can buy \\(20\\div4=5\\) gallons. Each gallon allows her to drive \\(32\\) miles, so she can drive\n\\[\n5\\times32=160\\text{ miles}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(160\\) miles, choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
